SUMMARY:Guided Walking Tour of Yorkville 
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Wednesday\, July 22nd**\, **join a Gu
 ided Walking Tour of Yorkville provided by the Royal Ontario Museum.** Evo
 lving from an 1800’s tollgate village at the edge of Toronto to an upsca
 le commercial destination\, see how this iconic neighbourhood has maintain
 ed its character despite being engulfed by the city. These Tours are guide
 d by docents\, and run rain or shine. However\, if the forecast calls for 
 rain\, I will make a call 3 hours prior if I will show up\, as others may 
 want to continue in the rain\, which the forecast has been off a lot recen
 tly.\n\n**Prepare for the walk:**\n\n* Walking shoes\n* Hat\n* Sunglasses\
 n* Water\n\n‐‐----‐----‐‐-------------‐-----------\n**COST:**\
 nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n‐‐----‐----‐‐-------------‐------
 -----\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes to confirm if you will join for food
 / drinks after**\n* A reminder will be sent the day before with my cell an
 d reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior and 
 cancellations may result in a No Show and impact future attendance\n\n**ME
 ETUP DETAILS:**\n**Meet at: 5:45pm at 1 Yorkville Ave (SW corner at Yonge)
 **\n**Tour location: We will then join the rest of the tour group at Yorkv
 ille Library at 22 Yorkville Ave.**\n**Tour starts: at 6pm**\n**Tour ends:
 ** ROM\, corner of Bloor St. and Queen’s Park (100 Queen’s Park\, Toro
 nto\n**Walk length: less than 2 hours**\nAfter: Head over to a local resta
 urant\n\nEnjoy and please post your Comments in the event after
