SUMMARY:Toronto Botanical Gardens Free Concert & Dance\, Pre-Guided Walkin
 g Tour + Dinner
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Thursday\, August 13th\, come to the 
 Toronto Botanical Gardens for a Free Concert with Classical Ballet and Con
 temporary Dance. You will have the option to join a Guided Walking Tour of
  the Gardens before\, and enjoy food and drink while there.** There will a
 lso be pre-show activities that night - **Discovery Cart** to learn about 
 plants\, **Plant/ Seed Swap**\, and an **Eco-station** to support their wa
 ste diversion and recycling program. This is an outdoor event and concerts
  proceed rain or shine. However\, if there is constant rain\, I will post 
 a comment maximum 3 hours before that I will not be attending\, and attend
 ees can still choose to stay for the concert. Chairs are provided\, first 
 come. If you plan to arrive late\, bring your own chair.\n\n**Concert with
  classical ballet and contemporary dance**\nLed by pianist Chris Au\, the 
 extraordinary musicians of *Joy of Music* perform a gorgeous array of conc
 ert pieces brought vividly to life by dancers from the worlds of classical
  ballet and contemporary dance. The sumptuous White Swan pas de deux is fe
 atured alongside new and recent works by esteemed Toronto choreographers J
 era Wolfe and Peggy Baker. A concert as lush and bounteous as the garden o
 f Joy of Music’s founder\, Mary Gore.\n\n**Pre-Guided Walking Tour**\nTh
 is walk will take you through the beautiful themed gardens and a stroll in
 to the beloved Edwards Gardens. You’ll learn about the history of these 
 gardens and all about pollinators\, the plants on display\, and the ecolog
 y of this area.\n\n**Music Series Host**\n**[Anwar Knight](https://anwarkn
 ight.com/)** is an award-winning Canadian broadcaster and environmentalist
  with an illustrious career spanning over two decades\, during which he he
 ld pivotal roles at some of Canada’s largest newsrooms.\n\n**The Dandeli
 on Café**\nGrab light bites or dinner on the patio overlooking the concer
 t venue (limited space). Thursday night menu includes Flank Steak\, Grille
 d Salmon\, Chicken Skewers\, Jack Fruit “Crab Cake” and special desser
 t features. The cafe also offers hot and cold drinks\, snacks\, and ice cr
 eam.\n\n**Discovery Cart**\nExplore plants\, wildlife\, and ecosystems thr
 ough short\, interactive activities and other weekly pre-show activities f
 rom 5 to 7 p.m.\n\n**Free Plant & Seed Swap**\nBring as many plants as you
  wish to trade. If there isn’t anything of interest on the table when yo
 u arrive\, add your plant(s) and take a ticket to redeem later when you se
 e something new you’d like to try. You can also borrow seeds from their 
 Seed Library for FREE!\n\n**COST**\nGuided Garden Tour: Adults $15/ Senior
 s $10 + taxes and fees (14 spots left). **[Purchase](https://www.eventbrit
 e.ca/e/tour-pre-concert-toronto-botanical-garden-tickets-1984152646979)** 
 your ticket in advance as it will likely sell out. Select Check availabili
 ty\, August 13\, 5:30 - 6:30 pm\, Adult/ Senior and finish your transactio
 n. After\, I highly recommend you select get tickets\, download and print 
 your tickets\, as it is too complicated to do this when you get there.\n\n
 Concert: Free\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Ye
 s confirming if you will join for the walk before.**\n* You can also just 
 show up at any of the meeting times below\n\nA reminder will be sent the d
 ay before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSV
 Ps close 1 day prior. Cancellations will result in a No Show and impact fu
 ture attendance.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for The Guided Walking Tour
  at: 5:20pm in front of the Entrance to the Toronto Botanical Gardens at 7
 77 Lawrence Ave. E.**\n\n**Walking Tour Start: 5:30**\n\nTour Length: 1 ho
 ur and ends back at the concert site\n\n**Meet me for Food/Drinks/Concert 
 at: 6:25pm in front of the Dandelion Cafe inside the Toronto Botanical Gar
 dens at 777 Lawrence Ave. E.** We will quickly find seats and take turns g
 etting food.\n\n**Concert Start: 7pm**\n\nConcert Length: 1 - 1.5 hours\n\
 nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after.
